From: Protector of Earth Recomp
Subject: [PATCH] SQRT.S: read the operand from the ft field

What broke:
  SQRT.S took the square root of $f[fs]. In the game's code fs is always 0,
  so every SQRT.S read $f0: 31 of Ben 10's 85 SQRT.S use another register
  and gave wrong results.

Why:
  On the R5900 the format is SQRT.S fd, ft (operand in ft, fs = 0), unlike
  MIPS IV's SQRT.S fd, fs (EE Core Instruction Set Manual; PCSX2 FPU.cpp
  SQRT_S uses _FtValUl_). The game's compiler encodes it that way: all 85
  SQRT.S in SLUS_216.61 have fs = 0 (tools/analyzer, docs/findings/14 s.5).

The fix:
  FPU_SQRT_S(ctx->f[ft]) instead of FPU_SQRT_S(ctx->f[fs]).

How it was found:
  Test SqrtsReadsFt; counting the fields of the game's SQRT.S.

diff --git a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/fpu_translator.cpp b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/fpu_translator.cpp
index 435db3a..f53e63c 100644
--- a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/fpu_translator.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/fpu_translator.cpp
@@ -58,7 +58,9 @@ namespace ps2recomp
                                    "ctx->f[{}] = FPU_DIV_S(ctx->f[{}], ctx->f[{}]); }}",
                                    ft, fd, fs, ft);
             case COP1_S_SQRT:
-                return fmt::format("ctx->f[{}] = FPU_SQRT_S(ctx->f[{}]);", fd, fs);
+                // On the R5900, SQRT.S fd, ft takes its operand from the ft field (fs is 0),
+                // unlike MIPS IV's SQRT.S fd, fs (EE Core manual; PCSX2 FPU.cpp SQRT_S uses Ft).
+                return fmt::format("ctx->f[{}] = FPU_SQRT_S(ctx->f[{}]);", fd, ft);
             case COP1_S_ABS:
                 return fmt::format("ctx->f[{}] = FPU_ABS_S(ctx->f[{}]);", fd, fs);
             case COP1_S_MOV:
